BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River History Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T120000
UID:8a9ef13436a8694b298398929f3ac2c9@thefloathousepetaluma.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63
 02d39abd02437a9e9f0276/1769554819341-GSKOMFLWE47GHOKQMBJW/Petaluma+River+H
 istory+Paddle+2026+for+squarespace+calendar+%281500+x+1000+px%29.png
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma River History Paddle The Petaluma River is the reason
  there’s a city here. Long before highways and railroads\, this tidal wa
 terway was the region’s saltwater highway —a working river that powere
 d Petaluma’s rise and connected Sonoma County’s farms and businesses t
 o San Francisco\, the Gold Rush\, and markets around the world. On this tw
 o-hour\, gentle guided paddle \, history comes alive through storytelling 
 from multiple points of view. You’ll paddle in stable sit-on-top kayaks 
 with an experienced\, costumed guide\, while costumed actors on shore step
  into the lives of real Petalumans who once depended on the river for thei
 r livelihood. Hear stories from people who worked the egg trade\, ran mess
 ages between businesses\, managed boarding houses\, and built enterprises 
 that fueled a growing city. As you move through downtown and along histori
 c riverbanks\, you’ll gain a deeper appreciation for the ingenuity\, ind
 ustrious spirit\, and daily lives that shaped Petaluma—and the river tha
 t made it all possible. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment an
 d instruction provided. Just bring your curiosity—and be ready to see Pe
 taluma through new eyes. $75/person. Includes everything\, even insight! R
 eserve your spot here! #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c { --stroke-style: none\
 ;--stroke-thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: initial\; 
 } #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c .sqs-html-content { --tweak-text-block-paddi
 ng: 6% 6% 6% 6%\; --tweak-text-block-padding: initial\; } #block-186fb3210
 b9d4444859c { mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend )\; border-radi
 us: var(--tweak-text-block-radius)\; } #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c { --twe
 ak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px\; } #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c { } 
 @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c { } } @
 media screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c .sqs-htm
 l-content { } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { }
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma\, 50 Water Street\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/events/petaluma-river-history-pa
 ddle-june-21-2026
X-SOURCE:The Floathouse Petaluma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to SUP: Build skills. Find flow. Love the river. 
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T110000
UID:29f65f0f4ed96644f6aacb15cbc9b1ba@thefloathousepetaluma.org
